[[31,63,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                receives the &#x27;door open&#x27; input signals\n              at pin 8 (left door) and pin 25 (right door) of connector E.</p><p>The Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                is connected,\n              via the CAN line, to the controls in the front door \n                              \n                              <strong>H44</strong>\n                              \n                               \n              according to the control logic described previously, which supplies\n              the two door courtesy lights \n                              \n                              <strong>G51</strong>\n                              \n                                and \n                              \n                              <strong>G52</strong>\n                              \n                               .</p><p>The unit \n                              \n                              <strong>H44</strong>\n                              \n                                is supplied by the\n              line protected by fuse F39 of the underdashboard control unit \n                              \n                              <strong>B2</strong>\n                              \n                               .</p><p>The &#x27;low battery voltage&#x27; signal which switches\n              off the courtesy lights if they are on, always arrives via the CAN \n              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3023163\">E1050</a>\n                              \n                               .</p>"]]